  "body": "Chrome 68 supports BigInt and also Node.js v10 supports it with `--harmony-bigint` flag. But console.log doesn't support BigInt in them.\r\n\r\nChrome 68\r\n\r\n```js\r\n> console.log(\"%d\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\nNaN\r\n> console.log(\"%i\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\nNaN\r\n```\r\n\r\nNode.js v10.7.0 with `--harmony-bigint`\r\n\r\n```js\r\n> console.log(\"%d\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\n1.1805916207174113e+21\r\n> console.log(\"%i\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\n1.1805916207174113e+21\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think expected result is \r\n\r\n```js\r\n> console.log(\"%d\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\n1180591620717411303424n\r\n> console.log(\"%i\", 1180591620717411303424n)\r\n1180591620717411303424n\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, [spec](https://console.spec.whatwg.org/#formatting-specifiers) shows `%d or %i` uses `%parseInt%(element, 10)` for type conversion.\r\nWhat specifier is the best for BigInt? Has this already been discussing?",
